==Notes==
* All draugr belong to the {{Faction|Creature Faction}} and the {{Faction|DraugrFaction}}. The [[#Draugr Thrall|Draugr Thrall]] belongs to the {{Faction|dunFolgunthurThrallFaction|nocat=1}} as well.
* Several spectral draugr can be found in [[Skyrim:Labyrinthian|Labyrinthian]] during the quest [[Skyrim:The Staff of Magnus|The Staff of Magnus]], along with [[Skyrim:Spectral Warhound|Spectral Warhounds]]. These draugr variations drop spectral weapons: [[Skyrim:Drainheart Sword|Drainheart Swords]], [[Skyrim:Drainblood Battleaxe|Drainblood Battleaxes]], and the [[Skyrim:Drainspell Bow|Drainspell Bow]].
* For draugr at rest (in a niche or standing) in a catacomb a good rule of thumb is that if it is wearing clothes, it can come to life and attack. 
* Draugr that are naked and nearly skeletal, draugr on the second tier of niches, and draugr wrapped like mummies cannot come to life. These draugr act like burial urns and if you have the [[Skyrim:Prowler's Profit|Prowler's Profit]] ability from the [[Skyrim:Thieves Guild (faction)|Thieves Guild]] [[Skyrim:No Stone Unturned|Stones of Barenziah]] quest, they will contain gemstones.
*Draugr and Draugr Deathlords do not have a magic-using variant; they can only be archers, one-handed fighters or two-handed fighters. Hulking Draugr cannot be magic users, archers or two-handed melee fighters. Draugr Death Overlords can only be one-handed melee fighters and two-handed fighters. All non-named boss Draugr also cannot cast spells, and instead will be either a one-handed or two-handed melee fighter; boss Draugr also cannot belong to the archery class.
*If you manage to disarm a draugr (either through the [[Skyrim:Disarm|Disarm]] shout or the Disarming Bash perk in the [[Skyrim:Block|Block]] skill tree), they will have a unique animation for unarmed attacks and deal very low unarmed damage. If there is a replacement weapon around (such as an Iron Battleaxe), they will equip and use it, even if they weren't a two-handed melee fighter in the first place.
*Halldir's clones and Jyrik Gauldurson are the only two Draugr in the game that use all elements (fire, frost and shock) against you. All other spellsword Draugr use frost magic exclusively.
*Red Eagle, Warlord Gathrik, and Yngol may appear as [[Skyrim:Dragon Priest|Dragon Priests]] at higher levels. This is determined by the [[Skyrim:Radiant|radiant]] system.
*The two Draugr that you can make in the [[Skyrim:Trophy Room|Trophy Room]] of your homestead are the same two models seen in the [[Skyrim:Loading Screens|loading screens]].

